# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# StockPulse — Environment Variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE:
#   1. Copy it:   cp .env.example .env
#   2. Fill in your values in .env
#   3. .env is git-ignored — it will NEVER be committed to GitHub
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── FINNHUB (required) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used for: real-time quotes, earnings, news, analyst Buy/Hold/Sell consensus
# Free tier: 60 requests/minute
# Get your key: https://finnhub.io/dashboard
VITE_FINNHUB_KEY=your_finnhub_api_key_here


# ── POLYGON (required) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used for: historical OHLCV chart candles (price chart)
# Free tier: daily bars, up to 5 requests/minute
# Get your key: https://polygon.io/dashboard
VITE_POLYGON_KEY=your_polygon_api_key_here


# ── SCHWAB OAUTH (Vercel dashboard only — see instructions below) ─────────────
#
# These three variables power the "Connect Schwab" button for real-time quotes
# and analyst price targets. They must be added to Vercel's Environment
# Variables dashboard — NOT stored in this file for production use.
#
# For local testing with `vercel dev`, you may uncomment them here.
# WARNING: Never commit this file with real Schwab values filled in.
#
# Where to find each value:
#   SCHWAB_CLIENT_ID     → developer.schwab.com → Your App → "App Key"
#   SCHWAB_CLIENT_SECRET → developer.schwab.com → Your App → "App Secret"
#   SCHWAB_REDIRECT_URI  → Must EXACTLY match the Callback URL in your Schwab app
#                          Format: https://your-app.vercel.app/api/auth/callback
#
# SCHWAB_CLIENT_ID=your_schwab_app_key_here
# SCHWAB_CLIENT_SECRET=your_schwab_app_secret_here
# SCHWAB_REDIRECT_URI=https://your-app.vercel.app/api/auth/callback


# ── GITHUB ACTIONS SECRETS (GitHub repo settings — not in this file) ─────────
#
# These are added in GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions.
# They are listed here for reference only — do not add them to .env.
#
#   VERCEL_TOKEN        → vercel.com/account/tokens → Create Token
#   VERCEL_ORG_ID       → Run `vercel link` then read .vercel/project.json
#   VERCEL_PROJECT_ID   → Same file as above
